WEBVTT

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.230
It's so hot!

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.940
I can't believe we have to weed and 
water the garden today, of all days.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.910
End-of-Semester Cleaning

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.390
I'll hold the dustpan!

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:15.240
No, I'm holding the dustpan!

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.870
I'm holding the dustpan!

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.370
Okay, let's do it together.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.720
I can do it myself.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.870
Aww...

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.270
So hot...

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.710
The weather's supposed to stay 
sunny like this for a while.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.370
Seriously?

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:37.680
We get in trouble at home for leaving 
the air conditioner on all the time.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.100
It's gonna be hell.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:41.850
But summer vacation starts in two days.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.080
I do look forward to summer vacation.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.880
I just hate the heat.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.110
I'm also going to hate the 
report card I get tomorrow.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:53.060
Well, let's get the watering 
and weeding done,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.660
and get back to the classroom.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.530
Yeah, let's.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.250
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.780
<i>I've hardly ever been alone 
with Hotarun before.</i>

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.400
<i>Huh... What should I talk about?</i>

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.530
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.530
<b>We Made Friends with Fireflies</b>

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.240
<i>I never felt weird when we 
were with everyone else...</i>

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.710
<i>What's a topic Hotarun 
might be interested in?</i>

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.330
<i>Fashion, maybe?</i>

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.670
<i>I can't think of a single thing to say.</i>

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.210
So, hey, Hotarun...

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.780
Yes? What is it?

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.340
Have you seen the anime <i>Pretty Cute</i>?

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:30.920
Yes, I saw it!

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.390
It was on a long time ago, right?

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:36.360
The girls who fight for love 
and justice, Pretty Cute!

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.760
On the pretty scene!

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.320
Oh, that's Pretty Cute's signature line!

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.780
My true name is Dirty Cute!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.780
I'll crush you all...

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.220
...to smithereens and toss you 
out with the pretty trash!

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.940
Oh, it's Pretty Cute from the last episode!

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.230
Wasn't that awesome?

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:55.710
I remember!

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:58.670
I was so surprised when the final 
enemy was the main character.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.550
Yeah! She revealed her true form in the end!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.870
I only saw the last few episodes 
of that anime, though.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.810
Then a new series called <i>Twinkle Sisters</i> 
replaced it, remember?

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.460
Right...

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:16.730
I like Pretty Cute, too, 
but that one is my favorite!

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:19.680
Oh...

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.300
Which character was your favorite?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:27.630
Oh, mine was Twinkle Black!

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:31.090
You know, she always distanced 
herself from the main character,

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:32.680
but she was really strong!

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:35.000
I kind of wanted to be 
like her at one time...

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:36.710
Yeah!

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:39.210
<i>What do I do now?</i>

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:43.340
I will color all evil beings black!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.480
She was so cool when she said that

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.870
<i>Hotaru's so excited, it's hard to 
tell her I only know the show title.</i>

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:48.180
and ran to help the main character!

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:49.300
<i>I've gotta change the subject...</i>

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.600
And the time they went 
to the Twinkle Planet...

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.290
Uh, b-by the way, Hotarun...

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.270
What is it?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:56.400
You know, Kazu-nee...

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.500
Oh! Yuuhi Kazuho, the one 
who transforms into Orange!

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.680
She's the main character's senpai!

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:02.530
<i>There's a Kazu-nee in the anime, too?!</i>

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.960
Is Orange your favorite?

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.450
She was so cool as the 
caring big sister type!

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.780
I can understand why you like her!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:11.390
<i>She understood!</i>

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:14.250
<i>I don't even have a clue, 
but she understood!</i>

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.050
R-Really?

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.460
Uh, I'm changing the subject here,

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.160
but I got these new indoor shoes, and...

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.250
That's right!

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.650
Orange always hit people

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.970
on the head with an indoor 
shoe when she corrected them!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.480
Like, "whack"!

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:28.960
So they got worn out

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.870
and she got new ones partway 
through the series!

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.400
So I was watching TV yesterday, and...

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.010
Oh! You watched the rerun yesterday, too?

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:41.350
I just had to watch it! It was so nostalgic!

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:44.480
Uh, no, this ramen show...

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:49.620
Oh! Yeah, the battle with the dark 
sun god, Ra Mentiptos, was amazing!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.550
And it was Orange's best moment, too!

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:58.870
Yeah! I like Orange, too, 
but I think Pink is my favorite!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.590
Huh? There was a Pink?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.180
Uh, maybe not so much Pink as Red...

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.690
Yeah! Red, the main character!

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:12.620
The main character was Green.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.520
Sorry. I didn't see that anime.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:28.700
Senpai, I'll leave the weeds I picked here.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.260
O-Okay.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.260
<i>I never found a good topic.</i>

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.930
Looks like we're done 
cleaning up the garden now.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:38.500
Y-Yep.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.460
It's so hot...

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:46.420
<i>If she were Nee-chan, I could tickle 
her ribs right now for a laugh,</i>

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:49.300
<i>but I can't imagine doing that to Hotarun...</i>

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:54.350
<i>There's a gecko on Hotarun's back!</i>

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:57.600
<i>If she notices, it won't be a 
discussion topic. It'll be chaos!</i>

00:06:58.250 --> 00:06:59.600
<i>I should just quietly...</i>

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:04.820
Whew! When it's this hot, 
I just want to dive in the river!

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:06.780
Ah, yeah...

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:09.670
I'm a little scared of diving, though.

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.820
Oh, really?

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.190
Cluck! Cluck, cluck, cluck!

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:19.160
When it's this hot, I just 
want to turn into a chicken!

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.530
Senpai?

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:25.200
Hotarun, look over there! 
A scarecrow's walking!

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.380
It's so cute!

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:29.340
H-Huh?

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:31.290
It doesn't bother you?

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.510
What do you mean?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.570
Well, I thought you'd hate stuff like that.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.870
What? But isn't it cute?

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.360
Do you not like lizards and things?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.320
That's a gecko, actually...

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.310
I'm totally fine with them, too.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.250
Hey, are you okay with newts, too, then?

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:50.320
Newts? I've heard of them...

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:54.930
Well, they're kind of 
like lizards and geckos,

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:56.510
but they live in water.

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.550
What? In water?

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:02.420
Th-That's amazing! 
They're like Komodo dragons!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.170
Oh, but they're small, so I 
guess they're Komodo lizards!

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.540
No, they're not lizards...

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:10.510
I think I just met the aggressive Hotarun!

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:14.160
I'll take you to a pond that 
has newts sometime, then.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.730
Oh, I'd love that!

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:18.810
A pond would have newt tadpoles, too.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:20.460
Even though they're not frogs?

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.450
Yeah, they're amphibians.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.600
Their tadpoles look sort of like axolotls.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:26.770
Wow!

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.400
So when should we go?

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.340
Could we go today?

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.860
I really want to see them now!

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:35.780
Okay, then we can go after we drop 
off our school stuff at home.

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:36.870
Okay!

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.830
Gecko! Gecko! Gecko! Gecko!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.750
There's a gecko!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:46.610
I'll crush that gecko to smithereens 
and toss it out with the trash!

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:49.220
Oh... It's Pretty Cute 
from the last episode.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.050
Curse you! I'm bigger than you ar—

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.150
Hey, Ren-chon, Hotarun.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.120
Nattsun, what are you 
fishing for in the grass?

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.450
The answer is...

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.950
Onions!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.370
Onions?

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.930
They've been biting like crazy.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:24.860
Huh?

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:26.770
You can fish for onions?!

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.800
Oh, you didn't know?

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:31.210
When you talk about fishing, 
it's gotta be onion fishing!

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:33.920
Me, too! I want to fish for onions, too!

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.630
I was kidding.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.850
What do you mean?

00:09:40.090 --> 00:09:42.770
I'm using the onion to catch katydids.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.690
You can catch them with onions?

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:45.980
You sure can.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:49.580
I'm not getting many though, 
so I was about to stop.

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.570
Wanna go do something?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.990
S-Sure. We were just talking 
about where we should go play.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.910
Yeah? Anything you want to do?

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.800
I wanted to fish for onions!

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:02.110
You can't.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:03.620
Then bug catching!

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.520
Bug catching, huh?

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.750
I just went to the newt pond 
with Hotarun the other day.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.110
That was a lot of fun.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.900
I don't have a bug net with me.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:16.990
What should we do?

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.870
Hotarun, Ren-chon, wanna eat some of this?

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:26.920
What is it?

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:28.750
It's called sorrel.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:31.310
If you peel it like this, you can eat it.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:35.320
It might be a little tough 
since it's summer, though.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:37.520
You can eat this plant?

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:41.570
Nee-nee told me not to eat grass 
I found on the side of the road.

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:43.280
You can just chew on it, then.

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:47.330
It's sour!

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:50.710
It's not half bad, though.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.130
Right?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.960
Nattsun, you can fish for 
katydids and everything.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.710
You know a lot of stuff!

00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.090
You really do.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.050
Like the difference between geckos and newts.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.490
You think so?

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:03.390
Also, if you throw a pebble near a bat,

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.280
it'll think it's food and come down for it,

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:09.360
and sweetfish smell like watermelon.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:10.460
Wow!

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:14.220
More stuff I didn't know! You're amazing!

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.690
What do you call someone like that again?

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:19.190
Uh, a genius?

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.750
Now you're getting a big head.

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:22.660
Shut up!

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.320
Well, whatever...

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.610
If we're going bug catching, 
we should go to the shrine.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:28.120
'Kay!

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:28.120
Okay.

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:40.550
How will we catch bugs without a net?

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.010
We'll catch cicadas.

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:45.980
Cicadas?

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:47.610
Without a net?

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:49.180
Yep. We'll catch cicadas.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.140
I get it!

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:53.060
You mean the meat from a fish's back!

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.020
No, I don't.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.770
Th-Then... A semi-auto-er?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.620
Semi-auto-er?!

00:11:58.620 --> 00:11:59.530
No.

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.790
What are we doing, then?

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:04.890
We're just going to use a 
different method to catch them.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.680
There's one!

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:09.560
What's this hole?

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.250
There's a cicada in there.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.390
Cicadas fly.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.210
They don't live in places like this.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.050
Don't believe me, huh?

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:19.800
Ren-chon, is there still 
water in that thermos?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.480
I didn't drink any yet.

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:22.760
What are you going to do?

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.430
C-Cicada...

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:28.960
Won't it drown?

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.640
It'll be fine.

00:12:44.270 --> 00:12:45.740
Something's coming out!

00:12:57.560 --> 00:12:59.170
Who are you?

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:01.380
That's a cicada nymph.

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:02.790
That's a...

00:13:02.790 --> 00:13:06.080
It does look just like a cicada shell!

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:14.060
I've never seen a cicada nymph before!

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.480
Me, either!

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.360
Yeah? Good for you two.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.540
I'm going to call it Hand-to-Mouth.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:24.070
Don't give a cicada that name.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:30.400
Well, we caught a cicada. 
Guess we should head back.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.760
Nattsun, can you keep nymphs?

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:38.370
Well, once they come out of the 
ground, they molt within the day,

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:42.770
so I guess you should just keep it 
until it molts, then let it go.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.540
You really do know a lot, Natsumi-senpai.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.050
I see you in a new light!

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.480
I know, right?

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:52.430
I just had a good idea!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.730
I'm going to observe the cicada molting 
for my summer free research project.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.160
Oh, I'd like to do that, too!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.400
Okay, we'll observe it together.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.280
I haven't done any of my homework at all...

00:14:05.420 --> 00:14:07.280
But if you don't work on it 
bit by bit over the summer,

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.410
won't it be harder at the end of the break?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.570
I know, but...

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:15.370
Well, "play while you have 
the chance" is my motto.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.040
What, Ren-chon?

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.300
Were you about to call me 
Hand-to-Mouth, like that cicada?

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.370
No.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:29.390
If anything, you're a Katydid.

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:43.680
Cicadas may have short lives,

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:46.780
but they spend them flying in 
the sky and eating sweet nectar.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.370
R-Renge-san?

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:56.060
Jeez, we're all together for 
once, and all we do is study?

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:57.290
This is no fun!

00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.600
I can't take any more.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:02.380
Let's forget about homework and go play.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:06.720
It's only been ten minutes since we started.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:08.600
And with that sun beating down,

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.340
it's too hot to play, anyway.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.440
Oh, if you want to play,

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:17.190
my parents are shopping today, 
and they said they'd buy some fireworks.

00:15:17.190 --> 00:15:18.570
Would you like to join me?

00:15:18.570 --> 00:15:19.840
A 180cm shell?!

00:15:19.840 --> 00:15:21.150
That's way too big.

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:23.260
Ooh! Fireworks, fireworks!

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.390
Hotarun, can I light them with you?

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:28.790
Me, too! I wanna light fireworks, too!

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:30.030
Me, too!

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.490
Yes, of course!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:36.180
Nattsun, let's finish our homework 
in time for fireworks tonight!

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.700
All right!

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.810
Okay, it's still early,

00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:42.260
so we'll split up for a bit 
after we finish the homework,

00:15:42.260 --> 00:15:45.670
have dinner, and then 
head to Hotaru's house.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:46.900
Does that sound okay?

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.430
Sure! I'll be waiting at home, then.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:55.400
I'm glad the sky's clear!

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:57.230
We'll meet Renge first.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.060
Nattsun!

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.020
Oh, it's Ren-chon and Kazu-nee.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.780
Hey!

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:06.780
You're coming with us, too?

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:09.490
Yep. I'm your chaperon.

00:16:10.180 --> 00:16:12.720
I wanna see skyrockets!

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.080
That sounds awesome!

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.470
Or if there are no skyrockets,

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:17.650
the ones that look like a shower would work!

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:20.110
Those are awesome, too!

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:27.370
Nattsun, let's see whose sparkler 
stays lit the longest!

00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.910
You won't beat me!

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.720
Hey! We're here, Hotarun!

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:37.510
Wh-What's wrong, Hotarun?

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.380
W-Well...

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:43.270
The store they went to was out of fireworks,

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.230
so they hardly got any...

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:48.930
I'm sorry!

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:51.380
I know you were all so excited about this!

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:53.900
And Ren-chon and Komari-senpai 
and Natsumi-senpai

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.860
all said you wanted to light fireworks!

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:59.320
No, it's totally fine!

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:03.000
Uh, but if they "hardly" got any, 
does that mean they got something?

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.290
This cylinder thing was the only one left...

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:09.630
Hey, that's the really 
flashy kind! Let's use it!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.500
R-Really?

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.260
Here. Be careful.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:17.180
A-All right!

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:20.670
I'm gonna light it now!

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:48.080
Um...

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.750
Hotaru, any other fireworks?

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.710
That was the only one.

00:17:56.870 --> 00:18:02.670
Ah, but... That was more 
fun than I expected...

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:04.210
I guess...

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:09.200
Yeah! It was lots of fun!

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.430
R-Right, right!

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:14.370
I haven't seen a parachute 
firework in ages. It was cool!

00:18:14.370 --> 00:18:16.650
Yeah! Thanks for inviting us!

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:19.900
M-Me, too! I had fun, too!

00:18:19.900 --> 00:18:22.430
I was really excited about the fireworks!

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:25.250
I was excited ever since 
you told us about it!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:31.030
So it was really fun doing fireworks 
with... everyone... today...

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.720
You didn't do anything wrong, Hotarun.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:42.040
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry, everyone!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:45.190
Um... Looks like this ended 
sooner than I was expecting.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:44.100
You don't have to cry! 
It's nothing to cry about, really!

00:18:44.590 --> 00:18:47.770
Hotarun, it's fine! Okay? Okay?!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:49.770
There's still plenty of time. 
Maybe I'll go for a walk.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:52.610
Where are you going, Kazu-nee?

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.880
Oh, not far.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:57.280
Hey, hear that? She's going for a walk.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:59.490
I don't know where, 
but we might as well go, too.

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:06.720
Hey, how far are we going? 
This goes to the woods.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:08.720
Don't worry about it.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.860
I wonder where we're going.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:12.310
No idea...

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:28.020
Ah, here we are. This is it.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.100
Disembodied souls!

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.270
They're fireflies!

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:49.700
How did you know about this place, Kazu-nee?

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.820
Huh? I thought you guys would know about it.

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:56.380
I guess you wouldn't come 
out here at night, though.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.730
There are so many Hotaruns!

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:01.540
Hotarun, let's get a closer look!

00:20:01.540 --> 00:20:02.590
O-Okay!

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.790
Koma-chan, come with us!

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:07.190
Hey, wait up!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.370
They're so shiny.

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:32.910
"Shiny"?

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:36.170
Hey! Look what we got!

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:39.180
If we wet these leaves in 
the river and hold them up,

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:41.400
maybe the fireflies will 
come to drink the water.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.070
I wanna try!

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:44.640
Me, too!

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.830
You think they'll come to us?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.330
I'll keep trying until they do.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.400
Oh, look, they're coming!

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:45.650
Hotarun made friends with a firefly.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:54.630
We didn't get to light fireworks, 
but we got to see some.

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:58.100
Yeah. Firefly fireworks.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:21.550
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:43.450
<i>Come on, dive in!</i>

00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:45.550
<i>She sent me a letter!</i>

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:48.520
<i>Hika-nee, say "goo-goo"!</i>

00:23:49.750 --> 00:23:50.570
<i>Goo...</i>

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:53.570
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:53.570
<b>We Bravely Dove In</b>

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:56.080
<b>Non Non Biyori
Repeat</b>

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:56.080
Photo: Canopus

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:56.080
Please Watch Again
